+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -2,6 +2,255 @@
 
 ## Unreleased
 
+- Keep active audio channels playing when repeated pan/frequency settings do not
+  change their values; clear the previous owner's pitch override on channel reuse.
+- Interpret word comparisons, TEST AL immediate, x87 memory comparisons and
+  FNSTSW AX using the shared flags/FPU model. Decode reachable instructions
+  through a worklist, including backward edges into previously skipped blocks.
+
+- Reuse at most 32 retired guest callback checkpoints per host thread while
+  retaining stable heap addresses for SEH and nested callbacks. Set
+  `RECOMP_CALLBACK_POOL=0` to compare the allocation path.
+- Apply queued host event completions before testing a wait, including a
+  zero-time poll, independently of the sampled import checkpoint.
+- Keep DirectSound buffer peak scans and first-play messages behind the
+  existing bounded audio trace. Normal playback does not scan PCM for logging.
+- Resolve resumable RET behavior at compile time when the game configuration
+  is available. Retain the runtime fallback for other translation units.
+- Expose the upstream QPC scaling diagnostic with finite multipliers from 1
+  to 8. Normal timing remains exact; scaling changes simulation pacing.
+
+- Prepare configured hosted game files automatically in browser storage, using
+  streamed, verified transfer chunks and resumable file imports. Check required
+  DLLs and normalize their names during folder imports before marking them ready.
+
+- Bound pointer-locked menu coordinates to the actual guest client size,
+  including Direct3D clients resized without a DirectDraw mode notification.
+  Keep locked clicks and wheel events at that same virtual cursor instead of
+  remapping the browser's fixed absolute position.
+
+- Send WM_MOUSEMOVE for pointer-locked motion as well as DirectInput counts,
+  letting menus show and update their software cursor while the OS cursor is
+  hidden. Respect consumed motion and deliver both paths under the scheduler baton.
+
+- Bound launcher status requests and report worker failures instead of leaving
+  the library waiting indefinitely. Allow retrying a failed status check without
+  importing again; long-running imports keep their existing timing behavior.
+
+- Capture the browser pointer on a canvas click and publish lock changes without
+  touching guest state on the UI thread. Deliver relative SDL mouse counts under
+  the scheduler baton, preserving camera motion past the absolute cursor edges.
+  Escape or focus loss releases the pointer; another click captures it again.
+
+- Explicitly destroy owned WebGPU textures when their last open encoder has
+  submitted, allowing GPU memory reclamation without waiting for JavaScript
+  garbage collection. Keep imported resources and browser canvas drawables
+  under their existing ownership rules. Report tracked texture creation and
+  destruction counts with performance diagnostics.
+
+- Add opt-in read-only scalar observations (`RECOMP_PERF_WATCH`) to the
+  existing performance report. Validate up to eight address/width pairs and
+  reject malformed or out-of-arena requests before reading guest memory.
+
+- Add opt-in bounded WebGPU vertex/index buffer renaming
+  (`RECOMP_D3D9_RENAME_BUFFERS=1`). Snapshot small rewritten buffers at distinct
+  ring offsets instead of submitting an open render pass, then restore their
+  persistent backing after submission in queue order. Retain the old barrier
+  for large updates; report renames and remaining buffer barriers. Honor
+  `RECOMP_D3D9_STATS=0` as disabled.
+- Add an opt-in persistent bind-group cache
+  (`RECOMP_D3D9_PERSIST_GROUP_CACHE=1`), retaining exact existing bindings
+  across Present. Keep the 4096-entry bound and invalidate before releasing
+  texture views, including on texture replacement or render-target rescaling.
+- Avoid callback TLS depth queries during resumable dispatch when no SEH
+  checkpoints exist. Retain registration, orphaning and adoption for live frames.
+
+- Add an experimental bounded read-path cache (`RECOMP_READ_PATH_CACHE=1`).
+  Reuse successful normalized path resolutions across repeated opens while
+  retaining independent file descriptors and on-demand contents. Invalidate
+  with existing file mutation, root and overlay changes; never cache writes or
+  missing paths. Measure complete CreateFile time in opt-in `perf-files` output.
+
+- Add opt-in WebGPU ring upload batching (`RECOMP_D3D9_BATCH_UPLOADS=1`):
+  stage distinct draw allocations and upload each used buffer prefix before
+  its existing queue submission. Preserve submission barriers and count actual
+  ring uploads separately from logical allocations for browser A/B checks.
+
+- Extend opt-in performance diagnostics with guest ReadFile throughput/read
+  wall time, outer interpreter calls/instruction counts, renderer encoding,
+  presentation wait and fixed-function preparation. Keep clocks and atomic
+  timing counters off without RECOMP_PERF_STATS=1. Show ten sampled callers.
+  Refresh refusal tests to exercise unsupported blending and invalid texture
+  operations rather than the lighting and multiply-add paths now implemented.
+
+- Add an opt-in WebGPU per-frame bind-group cache for browser performance
+  comparisons (`RECOMP_D3D9_FRAME_GROUP_CACHE=1`). Reuse bindings across
+  intermediate queue submissions; clear them at Present and before texture
+  views are retired, and cap retained entries. Default behavior is unchanged
+  until browser measurements validate rendering and performance.
+
+- Decode F6 /0 byte TEST with an immediate in the bounded interpreter,
+  including high-byte registers and SIB memory operands, without modifying
+  the tested operand or reading beyond its one-byte width. Accept the ModRM
+  dword INC/DEC forms using the existing carry-preserving execution path.
+
+- Stage only the web module referenced by the player, its resource package and
+  worker scripts. Keep diagnostic executables and linked/debug Wasm backups in
+  the build output instead of duplicating them into the served site.
+
+- Decode byte SHL/SHR/SAR, absolute byte MOV and byte group-1 immediates in the bounded
+  interpreter. Preserve neighboring bytes and high register bits, reuse
+  width-specific flag helpers, and keep ADC/SBB and unsupported prefixes refused.
+
+- Treat a standalone DirectShow graph (CoCreateInstance(CLSID_FilterGraph),
+  RenderFile, IMediaControl::Run and an IMediaEventEx notify window) as an
+  ownerless player: without a multimedia stream behind it there is no video to
+  decode or show, and its single completion event is announced through the
+  notify window as soon as the graph runs, so boot paths parked at "the movie
+  is over" advance on the guest's own message pump.
+
+- Hand DirectDrawCreateEx the version 7 factory: the same object as the legacy
+  factory through the v7 view, with the v7-only mode-test pair named as the
+  only extra stubs, older interfaces still routed through DirectDrawCreate
+  plus QueryInterface, and the refusal cases (aggregation, non-v7 IIDs)
+  preserved.
+
+- Round out the early D3D9 device surface: enumerate era-standard adapter
+  display modes so the game's 800x600x32 default exists in the list, return
+  the real render target from GetRenderTarget instead of an untouched
+  out-pointer, and bind or query FVFs through real declarations whose failed
+  validation leaves the previous binding intact.
+
+- Implement fixed-function flat shading (D3DRS_SHADEMODE = D3DSHADE_FLAT): the
+  gate accepts it into the same shader pair, the WebGPU renderer declares the
+  two colour varyings `@interpolate(flat)` in both stages, the CPU rasterizer
+  draws each triangle in its first vertex's colour, and the Metal and Vulkan
+  renderers refuse such draws rather than interpolate colours wrongly. Flat
+  shading keeps the first-vertex provoking rule of triangle lists and strips;
+  a triangle fan follows the WebGPU hardware rule (its apex) instead of the
+  Direct3D 9 fan rule (its second vertex), a documented deviation.
+
+- In resumable images, return cross-function direct JMP continuations to the
+  dispatcher instead of recursively calling their generated native bodies.
+  Split loops retain their guest state without accumulating native frames.
+  Add opt-in live profiling windows and bounded owner-thread depth reports.
+  Keep main-executable recovered-body audits out of auxiliary DLL translation.
+
+- Strip the trailing spaces and periods of every path component before
+  resolving a guest file name, matching Win32: names like "DATA\DEFAULT.IDE "
+  taken verbatim from game data files open the plain file instead of being
+  reported as missing.
+
+- Decode byte/word MOVSX and MOVZX to 32-bit registers and bounded 16-bit
+  register/memory MOV in the fallback interpreter. Keep the first player
+  failure visible when secondary worker or network errors arrive.
+
+- Execute bounded 32-bit XCHG, SHL/SHR/SAR and signed EDX:EAX IMUL in the
+  fallback interpreter, sharing the translated CPU's shift/multiply flags.
+  Support byte-register immediate MOV and decode-only startup diagnostics.
+
+- Expose the 3D listener on primary DirectSound buffers created with CTRL3D,
+  preserve buffer lifetime through listener references, and reject listener
+  queries on secondary buffers. Use the 64-byte DS3DLISTENER parameter record.
+
+- Map all verified auxiliary DLLs before binding any PE import table. Resolve
+  executable-to-DLL and DLL-to-DLL named/ordinal imports against guest exports
+  regardless of configuration order, and retain the bound reload snapshots.
+  Register the DirectSound8 COM device class and correct its interface IID so
+  an original audio DLL can create and initialize it through CoCreateInstance.
+
+- Keep returning tail-dispatch continuations live when another truncated
+  listing ends at a call to the dispatcher. Accept exactly FVF-representable
+  explicit vertex declarations in the bounded fixed-function draw path.
+
+- Package the current generated symbol map in web builds even after a direct
+  translator run. Match exclusive Direct3D 9 window geometry to the back buffer
+  and restore it on windowed reset. Implement standalone vertex/pixel shader
+  creation, binding, retrieval and bytecode lifetime through real COM objects.
+
+- Refuse incomplete web imports before entering the engine and retain a bounded
+  on-screen boot log, including JavaScript, WebGPU and runtime startup failures.
+
+- Preserve guest state in diagnostics when interpreting an unknown jump fails
+  decoding, and stop partial interpreter faults in STRICT_UNKNOWN mode before
+  fabricating a zero result or restoring the caller stack.
+
+- Render a bounded unlit/prelit Direct3D 9 fixed-function subset using real
+  FVF declarations and synthesized SM2 shaders shared by the CPU and GPU
+  paths. Refuse unsupported lighting, fog and texture stages explicitly;
+  preserve programmable bindings/constants and correct CPU point/clamp
+  sampling and DX9 pixel centres. Verify COM draws and offscreen Wasm pixels.
+
+- Add a real generated-code headless PE startup probe with verified local image
+  loading, strict import refusal and opt-in live guest snapshots at strict halts.
+
+- Add an opt-in STRICT_UNKNOWN runtime mode that stops at untranslated
+  calls or failed interpreted execution, retaining live instruction bytes
+  and decoder diagnostics instead of continuing with a zero result.
+
+- Execute PUSHFD/POPFD image trampolines and x87 real-memory load/store and
+  arithmetic forms in the fallback interpreter using the translated CPU's
+  flag, stack, tag and rounding model.
+
+- Implement InitializeCriticalSectionAndSpinCount through the recursive guest
+  lock scheduler and IsProcessorFeaturePresent using the guest CPU contract,
+  with registered stdcall argument counts for dynamic CRT startup calls.
+- Add a diagnostic mode for all generated chunks that keeps backend register
+  allocation without expensive LLVM IR optimization, preserving the normal
+  optimization level of native runtime sources.
+
+- Make guest cursor snapshots optional when a game's mouse object hooks are
+  absent; keep ordinary window and DirectInput motion without borrowing
+  another game's cursor layout.
+- Allow explicitly selected generated chunks to compile at O1 for diagnostic
+  builds, preserving the normal optimization level of every other source.
+- Allow the native formatter to select first-party paths without reformatting
+  unrelated local work.
+
+- Gate game-specific frame-clock substitutions on all configured hook
+  addresses; games without them compile and retain ordinary host-clock reads.
+- Bound computed MOV-immediate/NOP/JMP-register targets only with original
+  bytes and no intervening entry; unknown reachable jumps invalidate opaque
+  branch proofs, while unreachable ones do not invent entry points.
+- Read file offsets from 32-bit guest OVERLAPPED structures, preserve the
+  appropriate handle position, publish status/count/event completion, and
+  implement GetOverlappedResult for completed reads. Complete host reads
+  before returning pending async requests; reject unsupported blocking
+  pending states explicitly. Overlapped writes are not implemented here.
+- Route INT3/INT 3 through the existing fatal breakpoint handler, instead of
+  the ignored generic interrupt hook; SEH breakpoint continuation is not modeled.
+- During recursive recovery, skip only locally proven XOR-self/JE/JNE edges;
+  revisit a conditional if another edge enters it with unknown flags.
+- Publish resumable CALL returns from reachable sites and propagate newly
+  introduced entries to a fixed point; omit proven-dead CALL return markers.
+- Avoid reparsing non-FS operands in SEH scans and reuse each scan's branch
+  target set without changing the chain-head checks.
+- Prove original adjacent XOR-reg-self/JE/JNE branches only with no alternate
+  branch entry or computed jump; retain XOR writes and flags, and remove
+  only CFG paths the proven branch makes unreachable. Preserve taken edges
+  at conditional listing gaps as well as their fallthrough edges.
+- Translate 32-bit ENTER frame construction with nested frame copies,
+  five-bit nesting levels and unchanged arithmetic flags; keep 16-bit ENTER
+  explicitly unsupported pending a reliable differential stack oracle.
+- Recover LOOP taken paths and translate ZF-dependent loop aliases plus JCXZ;
+  respect CX address-size overrides and preserve flags and upper ECX bits.
+- Support same-descriptor segment POPs in the fixed flat Win32 context, with
+  correct stack operand widths; reject descriptor changes and SS single-step
+  states explicitly rather than silently ignoring them.
+- Index the union of decoded table storage ranges during code-pointer scans;
+  preserve covered-entry priority and exclusive interval ends.
+- Accept audited per-call nonlocal dispatcher transfers in resumable-stack
+  translations; preserve original CALL execution and trap unexpected fallthrough.
+- Index normalized declared data/code intervals for large annotated corpora.
+
+- Translate FEMMS with the defined MMX-exit tag effects shared with EMMS.
+
+- Let game translation inputs classify audited embedded PE file buffers as data;
+  retain their bytes and omit their listings and pointer-scan roots.
+
+- Cache immutable instruction decoding across overlapping static recovery walks;
+  preserve caller-specific bounds and return independent instruction objects.
+
 - Allow native game adapters to place their own cursors at absolute touch
   positions in logical game pixels. Placement can discard pending DirectInput
   X/Y movement without losing button, wheel or keyboard input.
