diff --git a/docs/testing.md b/docs/testing.md
index bb8776b..9384b32 100644
--- a/docs/testing.md
+++ b/docs/testing.md
@@ -1,5 +1,18 @@
 # Testing
 
+`startup_win32_tests --callback-pool` and `--callback-no-pool` exercise
+69,032 callback entries, including nesting beyond the 32-checkpoint retention
+limit and nonlocal sentinel returns. They check caller ESP/EIP/depth restoration
+and report allocations/reuses. The CPU loop timing is not a browser FPS result.
+`--host-events` checks manual/automatic event polling across sampled import
+checkpoint phases without sleeps. `--performance-counter` checks exact normal
+ticks and rejects malformed or non-finite diagnostic clock multipliers.
+
+`RECOMP_QPC_SCALE=2` reproduces the upstream timing experiment. It changes the
+guest clock and must not be used to validate normal physics or synchronization.
+`RECOMP_CALLBACK_POOL=0` disables checkpoint reuse for an allocation A/B; the
+normal path retains at most 32 retired checkpoints on each owning host thread.
+
 Run checks appropriate to your change. Every suite's output belongs under ignored
 `build/`; requested tests must report failure rather than silently skip prerequisites.
 
@@ -12,6 +25,114 @@ Run checks appropriate to your change. Every suite's output belongs under ignore
 | `tools/test.py --mods` | Real loader/hooks/settings/native Options and replay contracts | Yes, plus translated archive |
 | `tools/test.py --gameplay` | Menu navigation, mode cycling, selection, movement and clean exit | Yes, plus translated archive |
 
+`startup_win32_tests` exercises CRT critical-section and processor-feature
+imports through the real registry and dispatcher without an image or window.
+It checks dynamic resolution, stdcall stack cleanup, recursive ownership and
+the guest CPU feature contract. Its Emscripten build runs under Node.
+
+`game_boot_probe` links the real generated executable and auxiliary modules,
+then calls the verified PE entry through `run_entry` with the scheduler and
+actual import adapters. Its null graphics/audio host makes this a CPU startup
+diagnostic, not browser rendering or gameplay acceptance. Build the target
+through `tools/build.py`'s build API for the selected game. For Emscripten, run
+`node <output>/game_boot_probe.js <verified-executable>`; NODERAWFS reads the
+local installation and the loader still verifies every configured image hash.
+`game_boot_probe <exe> --decode <hex-address>` validates a bounded original
+routine using the fallback decoder without executing it. This establishes
+instruction/branch coverage only, not correct execution of the game path.
+`game_boot_probe <exe> --cstring <hex-address> <text>` invokes a known
+two-argument guest string-copy/conversion routine with `(text, 0)`. It checks
+the returned text, ESP and callee-preserved ESI; select only a routine whose ABI
+and expected identity conversion for the supplied input were independently
+verified. It is a focused CPU regression check, not gameplay evidence.
+
+With `RECOMP_PROFILE=1`, `RECOMP_PROFILE_INTERVAL_MS=5000` logs the ten most
+sampled published caller indices in each window. Valid intervals are 1000–60000
+ms; absence leaves existing exit-only reporting unchanged. Shims and host waits
+are attributed to their guest caller. A crashed worker can leave its published
+slot stale, so repeated samples alone do not prove execution is still advancing.
+
+`RECOMP_PERF_STATS=1` also prints `perf-io`: guest ReadFile calls, bytes and
+wall time inside the host read, plus outer interpreter calls and executed
+interpreter instructions. Nested interpreter calls consume the same budget and
+are counted once; translated callees do not consume it. These counts are not
+exclusive CPU time. File open/seek costs and native codec I/O are outside the
+ReadFile measurement. `interp_tests --perf-counts` checks nesting, translated
+callees and decoder refusal accounting using synthetic code.
+
+`perf-files` measures the whole CreateFile adapter, including path resolution
+and the host open, separately from ReadFile. `RECOMP_READ_PATH_CACHE=1` opts
+into at most 1024 successful normalized read-path answers; directory-cache
+invalidation also clears these answers. Writes and misses are not cached.
+`startup_win32_tests --read-path-cache` exercises independent handles/offsets,
+normalization, delete/recreate, root changes and overlay invalidation using
+temporary synthetic files. Browser FPS and storage behavior still require a
+foreground run; sampler percentages include waits attributed to callers.
+
+`seh_tests --empty-dispatch` runs a focused synthetic dispatcher check without
+the full suite's subprocesses or non-resumable guest-call fixtures. It checks
+unchanged empty-dispatch registers, no callback-depth lookups, and adoption of
+a registration installed after repeated empty dispatches. The full suite is a
+separate check and is not covered by this argument.
+
+`RECOMP_D3D9_RENAME_BUFFERS=1` enables an experimental WebGPU upload path.
+Buffers up to 256 KiB can be snapshotted at immutable ring offsets, with a
+4 MiB snapshot budget per encoder. Submission restores their persistent data
+after the queued draws; larger updates keep the original submission barrier.
+`buffer_renames/frame` and `buffer_barriers/frame` expose activity. Both vertex
+and index bindings must be checked in foreground browser gameplay; CPU SEH
+checks and Wasm compilation do not establish GPU ordering or pixel equivalence.
+`RECOMP_D3D9_PERSIST_GROUP_CACHE=1` retains bindings across Present, implying
+the per-frame cache. It preserves the 4096-entry cap and clears before texture
+view retirement. Compare `new groups/frame` and rendering against the existing
+per-frame cache in the same scene; this option is also disabled by default.
+
+With `RECOMP_PERF_STATS=1`, `RECOMP_PERF_WATCH=300000:1,300001:2,300003:4`
+reports those guest scalars every performance window without changing them.
+Addresses are hexadecimal without a prefix; widths are decimal 1, 2 or 4.
+At most eight fields are accepted, and malformed/overflowing/out-of-arena
+lists disable all observations. Only the scheduler baton holder reads them.
+`startup_win32_tests --perf-watch` checks parsing, ranges, unaligned values,
+exact widths and unchanged guest bytes. Game-specific addresses belong in the
+game's investigation evidence, not in this generic runtime implementation.
+
+The WebGPU device explicitly destroys its own retired textures only after all
+open command encoders have submitted. Imported D3D resources remain externally
+owned, and canvas drawables are released without explicit destruction so the
+browser can present them. With PERF_STATS, every 1000 tracked destructions logs
+created/destroyed/outstanding counts. These exclude imported resources and
+canvas textures and are not a VRAM usage measurement. Validate long foreground
+menu/loading/gameplay runs, absence of allocation/validation errors, and bounded
+outstanding counts; a native build or V8 compile cannot validate that behavior.
+
+The WebGPU report separately measures queued encoding batches, the guest's
+synchronous Present wait and fixed-function shader preparation with this flag.
+Those intervals overlap and must not be summed. Counters are diagnostic only;
+their clocks and atomic increments are disabled in normal play.
+The same option records the last twelve logical callers at exponentially
+increasing depths (128, 256, 512...). These chains are copied by their owning
+thread, never by racing another thread's mutable guest stack.
+Both `RECOMP_STRICT_UNKNOWN` and `RECOMP_STRICT_IMPORTS` are forced on, so missing
+code, missing import implementations or unknown import signatures stop the run.
+Before entry, the probe checks every import from a configured mapped module in
+the executable and auxiliary DLLs against the real named/ordinal export table,
+including the IAT bytes retained for DLL reload. A mismatch fails the probe.
+`game_boot_probe <exe> --sound-factory <module> <export>` instead calls a mapped
+three-argument DirectSound creation export, checks HRESULT/output/stack, invokes
+GetCaps through the returned original COM vtable, and releases the object. This
+focused test also creates a primary CTRL3D buffer, queries its listener, releases
+the buffer reference, and checks 64-byte GetAllParameters/SetAllParameters through
+the original DLL vtables with a trailing canary. It uses translated DLL code;
+it does not verify audible playback. The DX suite additionally checks refusal
+on primary buffers without CTRL3D and secondary-buffer interface views.
+Use an external execution timeout. `RECOMP_PROBE_DUMP=<existing-dir>/halt` writes
+live main/auxiliary images, stack, TEB and register metadata before a strict
+halt. These private diagnostic binaries belong under ignored `build/`.
+Decoder refusals also invoke the snapshot hook before executing instructions.
+`interp_tests --strict-fault` is an expected-abort check: a decoded routine
+pushes two stack words before an invalid memory read, and strict mode must
+retain that fault state rather than manufacture a successful zero return.
+
