@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+# Bounded Direct3D 9 fixed-function support
+
+`dx/d3d9_ffp.cpp` prepares shader-model-2 bytecode for both existing rendering
+paths. Preparing a draw is transactional: an unsupported state returns a reason
+without changing the device's programmable shader bindings or constants.
+
+The initial supported formats are XYZ or XYZRHW, optional normal (XYZ only),
+packed diffuse/specular colours, and zero to eight float2 texture coordinate
+sets. FVF layout follows Microsoft's [FVF-to-declaration mapping](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/direct3d9/mapping-fvf-codes-to-a-directx-9-declaration).
+An explicit declaration bound with SetVertexDeclaration also works when its
+stream, offsets, types, methods and order exactly match one of these layouts.
+The adapter derives the equivalent FVF for shader synthesis while retaining
+the original declaration for the draw. Padded, reordered, multi-stream or
+otherwise unsupported declarations are refused rather than rearranged.
+XYZ uses row-vector world/view/projection multiplication. XYZRHW reconstructs
+clip coordinates from the current viewport and reciprocal W, bypassing those
+matrices and lighting. The GPU renderer applies its existing DX9 pixel-centre
+adjustment after the shader; it must not be applied again inside the synthesized
+shader. See Microsoft's [texel-to-pixel mapping](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/direct3d9/directly-mapping-texels-to-pixels).
+
+The pixel stage supports select-argument, modulate (including 2x/4x), add and
+subtract, with independent colour/alpha operations, diffuse/current/texture/
+texture-factor/specular arguments, complement and alpha replication. It honours
+the selected UV set. A null texture with COLORARG1 set to TEXTURE stops the stage
+cascade, following Microsoft's [texture blending rules](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/direct3d9/texture-blending).
+
+Fog is honoured per draw: the renderer evaluates linear, exponential and
+exponential-squared table fog from the raster depth, and a synthesized vertex
+shader writes the rasterizer fog factor for the per-vertex modes. Specular
+addition folds the vertex specular colour into the pixel stage when
+D3DRS_SPECULARENABLE is set. Lighting, vertex blending, automatic texture
+coordinate generation, texture transforms, TEMP stage results, point-size FVFs
+and non-float2 UV formats remain unsupported and are explicitly refused.
+The pre-existing CPU rasterizer also lacks clipping and a complete depth/stencil
+implementation; it cannot be represented as a complete software D3D9 device.
+Offscreen pixel tests establish the supported operations, not a game's startup,
+playability or performance.
